WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Section 608 of the Clean Air Act makes it illegal to knowingly vent refrigerant.
Fines up to $44,539 per day per violation. Technicians must be EPA 608 certified
to purchase refrigerant. Recovery is required before any repair that opens the

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Section 608: Clean Air Act provision regulating stationary refrigerant
equipment.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Venting Prohibition: Knowingly releasing refrigerant is illegal. Fines up to
$44,539 per day.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Violations result in personal fines, not
just company fines. You are personally liable.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Venting is illegal for ALL refrigerant types. And — Fines
apply to individuals not just companies

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

